WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:05.750 --> 00:00:09.000
- Hello everyone, it
looks like we are live

00:00:09.000 --> 00:00:11.990
and we're getting better
at starting on time.

00:00:11.990 --> 00:00:15.690
Thanks for joining us at
our lot daily live stream

00:00:15.690 --> 00:00:17.600
at our new time that we started yesterday

00:00:17.600 --> 00:00:20.750
now today at 12 Pacific through Eastern

00:00:20.750 --> 00:00:24.640
and many people are from
joining from all over the world.

00:00:24.640 --> 00:00:26.110
We're calling this a bit of a homeroom,

00:00:26.110 --> 00:00:28.350
because obviously in this
time of school closures

00:00:28.350 --> 00:00:30.590
and social distancing, people can use

00:00:30.590 --> 00:00:33.560
things like Khan Academy
at their own time and pace,

00:00:33.560 --> 00:00:34.800
but I think we all crave

00:00:34.800 --> 00:00:36.047
a little bit of social connection

00:00:36.047 --> 00:00:38.290
and a way to to realize that

00:00:38.290 --> 00:00:39.580
what we're going through,

00:00:39.580 --> 00:00:41.070
the whole world is going through

00:00:41.070 --> 00:00:44.970
and as as troubling is
the scenario we are in,

00:00:44.970 --> 00:00:49.740
as a civilization there's
the silver lining is

00:00:49.740 --> 00:00:52.330
we I think in some strange
way feel more connected

00:00:52.330 --> 00:00:55.650
and one real you know humanity

00:00:55.650 --> 00:00:58.280
is one group of people right now.

00:00:58.280 --> 00:01:00.410
So just for those of you
all this is the first time

00:01:00.410 --> 00:01:02.700
that you're attending
one of these live streams

00:01:02.700 --> 00:01:05.390
with this home homeroom
that we do every day,

00:01:05.390 --> 00:01:08.350
it's really a catch-all
for answering questions,

00:01:08.350 --> 00:01:09.560
getting announcements out there.

00:01:09.560 --> 00:01:12.660
Really just like homeroom
in real classrooms.

00:01:12.660 --> 00:01:15.230
And it's not just for
students, it's for parents,

00:01:15.230 --> 00:01:17.170
it's for teachers, it's for anyone else

00:01:17.170 --> 00:01:20.520
who has questions of any form.

00:01:20.520 --> 00:01:22.040
Just to get everyone up to speed

00:01:22.040 --> 00:01:24.380
on what the resources
that are already out there

00:01:24.380 --> 00:01:25.610
from Khan Academy,

00:01:25.610 --> 00:01:27.640
obviously for over a decade

00:01:27.640 --> 00:01:29.350
we've been building resources

00:01:29.350 --> 00:01:33.270
that start you as early as
pre-k our Khan Academy kids app

00:01:33.270 --> 00:01:37.110
the it's suitable for
students as young as three

00:01:37.110 --> 00:01:38.960
all the way up through the first grade,

00:01:38.960 --> 00:01:42.260
Common Core Standards
up through six year olds

00:01:42.260 --> 00:01:45.160
and then on the main Khan
Academy app or website

00:01:45.160 --> 00:01:47.690
you can for sure get
math from kindergarten

00:01:47.690 --> 00:01:48.750
all the way through middle school,

00:01:48.750 --> 00:01:51.620
high school and the core of college

00:01:51.620 --> 00:01:54.780
and also sciences at
the high school level,

00:01:54.780 --> 00:01:56.330
some humanities at the high school level

00:01:56.330 --> 00:01:58.030
and we just launched what we call a beta,

00:01:58.030 --> 00:01:59.650
which is almost like a pre-release

00:01:59.650 --> 00:02:02.930
of English and language
arts for grades 2 through 8.

00:02:02.930 --> 00:02:06.530
We also have free SAT practice
which is a partnership

00:02:06.530 --> 00:02:08.530
with a college board that's in reading,

00:02:08.530 --> 00:02:10.690
math and writing.

00:02:10.690 --> 00:02:13.510
And we also have topics
like economics and others

00:02:13.510 --> 00:02:16.030
that I mean I could I
could keep going on about.

00:02:16.030 --> 00:02:17.930
So those resources were always all there

00:02:17.930 --> 00:02:19.170
but as soon as we realized

00:02:19.170 --> 00:02:21.130
that the school closure
situation was happening

00:02:21.130 --> 00:02:22.180
a few weeks ago,

00:02:22.180 --> 00:02:24.160
we we realized we have to step up more,

00:02:24.160 --> 00:02:26.020
we have to provide more resources.

00:02:26.020 --> 00:02:27.934
So that's when we started the livestreams,

00:02:27.934 --> 00:02:31.140
we've been running teacher
and parent webinars

00:02:31.140 --> 00:02:33.860
to help teachers and parents understand

00:02:33.860 --> 00:02:36.740
what resources there are
and how to get started.

00:02:36.740 --> 00:02:39.420
We have also published a schedule,

00:02:39.420 --> 00:02:40.820
a little over a week ago

00:02:40.820 --> 00:02:43.660
that for students of different age groups,

00:02:43.660 --> 00:02:46.870
what could be an indicative
schedule for them,

00:02:46.870 --> 00:02:48.630
how you can structure their day

00:02:48.630 --> 00:02:50.440
leveraging resources from Khan Academy

00:02:50.440 --> 00:02:52.320
and other resources including

00:02:52.320 --> 00:02:54.840
you know dance videos
on YouTube for your PE

00:02:54.840 --> 00:02:57.210
or you might want to go
outside and run around

00:02:57.210 --> 00:02:59.880
or there might be some
form of reading lists.

00:02:59.880 --> 00:03:01.470
This week some of you all realize

00:03:01.470 --> 00:03:03.590
we just did it a couple hours ago.

00:03:03.590 --> 00:03:08.370
We are also experimenting
with doing academic webinars.

00:03:08.370 --> 00:03:11.290
So a few hours ago we ran our first one

00:03:11.290 --> 00:03:14.160
which was on algebra and
we focused on the topic

00:03:14.160 --> 00:03:14.993
of systems of equations

00:03:14.993 --> 00:03:17.270
and we had great you know
we had a thousand students

00:03:17.270 --> 00:03:19.290
participating and we're taking the video

00:03:19.290 --> 00:03:21.330
and we're gonna put it
on our YouTube channel

00:03:21.330 --> 00:03:23.220
and probably promote on
social media as well.

00:03:23.220 --> 00:03:24.700
So you'll at least see a recording of it

00:03:24.700 --> 00:03:26.670
and I hope many of you have a chance

00:03:26.670 --> 00:03:30.770
to join some of these future classes.

00:03:30.770 --> 00:03:32.610
So with that one thing I want to say

00:03:32.610 --> 00:03:33.900
you know where we're trying to put out

00:03:33.900 --> 00:03:36.740
all of these resources, but one question

00:03:36.740 --> 00:03:39.580
that we're getting from
a lot of parents is,

00:03:39.580 --> 00:03:43.160
they're just feeling a little
bit overwhelmed right now,

00:03:43.160 --> 00:03:45.090
how do they focus on things,

00:03:45.090 --> 00:03:47.700
you know are they doing a
disservice to their children

00:03:47.700 --> 00:03:49.270
if if they don't have everything

00:03:49.270 --> 00:03:50.640
all figured out just yet.

00:03:50.640 --> 00:03:52.700
And the one thing I want to
make very clear to you is

00:03:52.700 --> 00:03:55.810
no one has it all figured out just yet.

00:03:55.810 --> 00:03:58.220
Even in my own house you know

00:03:58.220 --> 00:04:01.470
I've figured out some what
for especially my older kids

00:04:01.470 --> 00:04:03.230
but my five-year-old we're figuring it out

00:04:03.230 --> 00:04:05.780
but it is getting day day by day better.

00:04:05.780 --> 00:04:06.950
And so I think the important thing

00:04:06.950 --> 00:04:08.520
to appreciate as a parent,

00:04:08.520 --> 00:04:10.430
there's a lot of things
going on right now,

00:04:10.430 --> 00:04:11.470
you're working from home,

00:04:11.470 --> 00:04:13.024
a lot of people in this situation

00:04:13.024 --> 00:04:15.470
where even they might
not be able to work now

00:04:15.470 --> 00:04:18.230
and then you have to there's
childcare as an issue.

00:04:18.230 --> 00:04:19.930
And so keep it simple,

00:04:19.930 --> 00:04:21.500
especially in the first week or two

00:04:21.500 --> 00:04:22.940
it's not the end of the world,

00:04:22.940 --> 00:04:25.460
if things are a little
bit less structured,

00:04:25.460 --> 00:04:26.880
if your kids if you're just having

00:04:26.880 --> 00:04:28.140
quality time with your kids

00:04:28.140 --> 00:04:30.780
or just whatever it takes
to get through the day.

00:04:30.780 --> 00:04:34.030
But I think as as we go on,

00:04:34.030 --> 00:04:36.240
try to just make sure that the kids get

00:04:36.240 --> 00:04:38.280
a little bit of a reading every day,

00:04:38.280 --> 00:04:39.580
a little bit of math every day.

00:04:39.580 --> 00:04:42.210
We have suggestions obviously
Khan Academy as a resource

00:04:42.210 --> 00:04:43.630
for both and there's reading lists

00:04:43.630 --> 00:04:45.670
for the on the reading side of things,

00:04:45.670 --> 00:04:46.690
you know if your kids are old enough

00:04:46.690 --> 00:04:47.900
encourage them to journal.

00:04:47.900 --> 00:04:50.870
And then over time you could
try to layer on more things,

00:04:50.870 --> 00:04:53.430
try to do more and more
of the types of schedules

00:04:53.430 --> 00:04:55.820
we've published, those schedules
are not meant to be rigid.

00:04:55.820 --> 00:04:57.970
They are meant to be evolving documents.

00:04:57.970 --> 00:04:59.890
We are evolving them
and you can adapt them

00:04:59.890 --> 00:05:01.930
to your own needs.

00:05:01.930 --> 00:05:03.930
But this session we wanna make it

00:05:03.930 --> 00:05:05.110
as interactive as possible.

00:05:05.110 --> 00:05:07.560
So I encourage everyone,
if you're on Facebook,

00:05:07.560 --> 00:05:10.870
YouTube, Twitter start
putting your questions in

00:05:10.870 --> 00:05:12.870
and we have a team of Khan Academy folks,

00:05:12.870 --> 00:05:13.900
we're gonna be looking at them

00:05:13.900 --> 00:05:15.110
and surfacing the questions,

00:05:15.110 --> 00:05:17.210
it looks like a lot of
people are thinking about.

00:05:17.210 --> 00:05:19.970
I also wanna introduce
my colleague Dan too,

00:05:19.970 --> 00:05:23.120
who's kind of co-hosting
this livestream today

00:05:23.120 --> 00:05:24.370
and we're gonna actually this is fun

00:05:24.370 --> 00:05:25.990
'cause we figured out the technology

00:05:25.990 --> 00:05:27.420
hopefully over the coming livestreams

00:05:27.420 --> 00:05:29.700
we'll be able to bring different guests in

00:05:29.700 --> 00:05:30.980
and people who can help out with this,

00:05:30.980 --> 00:05:35.050
but Dan's gonna help he's
in contact with the team

00:05:35.050 --> 00:05:36.410
that is surfacing the questions.

00:05:36.410 --> 00:05:40.470
So please please send
send in your questions.

