00:06:01.340 --> 00:06:04.010
or their you know whatever graduate

00:06:04.010 --> 00:06:07.700
requirements for high school
diplomas they might have.

00:06:07.700 --> 00:06:09.220
So that's where we could
support you right now.

00:06:09.220 --> 00:06:11.730
But it is a dream to one
day be able to connect

00:06:11.730 --> 00:06:13.140
to work on Khan Academy

00:06:13.140 --> 00:06:17.943
to you know real life
economic or academic outcomes.

00:06:20.220 --> 00:06:21.330
And Dan feel free to jump in.

00:06:21.330 --> 00:06:24.290
I see another question from
Facebook Shahla Karimi,

00:06:24.290 --> 00:06:27.210
says Salaam, I have
fifth grade first grade

00:06:27.210 --> 00:06:30.530
and something younger daughters,

00:06:30.530 --> 00:06:32.950
why when it's a little typo,

00:06:32.950 --> 00:06:34.710
they are all acting out

00:06:34.710 --> 00:06:36.610
and they are really emotional

00:06:36.610 --> 00:06:38.270
since they are home due to virus.

00:06:38.270 --> 00:06:39.700
How can I help them?

00:06:39.700 --> 00:06:41.210
Well shala that's a great question.

00:06:41.210 --> 00:06:43.030
I think right now there's probably

00:06:43.030 --> 00:06:45.420
about a billion parents
who are experiencing

00:06:45.420 --> 00:06:49.130
some version of what you're
experiencing including myself.

00:06:49.130 --> 00:06:51.100
So I think the first thing to realize

00:06:51.100 --> 00:06:52.810
is don't don't beat up on yourself

00:06:52.810 --> 00:06:55.020
and think it's just like
you're the only person

00:06:55.020 --> 00:06:57.360
who maybe you know your
kids are acting out.

00:06:57.360 --> 00:06:59.570
And especially you know if
they have to stay at home,

00:06:59.570 --> 00:07:00.920
and they're not getting

00:07:00.920 --> 00:07:03.320
as much social interaction as possible.

00:07:03.320 --> 00:07:05.040
I'm not a child psychology expert,

00:07:05.040 --> 00:07:06.950
I actually hope we can bring some in

00:07:06.950 --> 00:07:10.280
into these livestreams,
all I can tell you is

00:07:11.850 --> 00:07:14.750
try to leverage things
like video conferencing,

00:07:14.750 --> 00:07:15.780
if you have access to it

00:07:15.780 --> 00:07:18.030
so that they can connect
with their friends.

00:07:18.030 --> 00:07:20.140
We've been doing playdates at home,

00:07:20.140 --> 00:07:22.030
obviously with my youngest
who's five years old.

00:07:22.030 --> 00:07:26.140
We've been moderating his his playdates

00:07:26.140 --> 00:07:27.590
with some of his five-year-old friends

00:07:27.590 --> 00:07:28.650
which can get a little chaotic

00:07:28.650 --> 00:07:31.530
if you don't help them out a little bit,

00:07:31.530 --> 00:07:33.340
we've been ensuring that you know

00:07:33.340 --> 00:07:34.490
in this time of social distance

00:07:34.490 --> 00:07:37.540
you can still take walks and
still have exercise outside,

00:07:37.540 --> 00:07:39.710
you just have to keep
distance from other people.

00:07:39.710 --> 00:07:41.610
But we're we're being quite religious

00:07:41.610 --> 00:07:43.700
about making sure that we go outside

00:07:43.700 --> 00:07:46.420
at least twice a day if we
can even if it's raining.

00:07:46.420 --> 00:07:47.460
We're getting the umbrellas out

00:07:47.460 --> 00:07:49.000
and saying we're going for a walk.

00:07:49.000 --> 00:07:51.660
'Cause I think it's really
valuable to get that.

00:07:51.660 --> 00:07:54.320
And then I think what we're
seeing in our own household

00:07:54.320 --> 00:07:57.180
is still a little bit
interesting sometimes

00:07:57.180 --> 00:07:59.180
but just everyone is getting

00:07:59.180 --> 00:08:00.810
a little bit used to this new normal

00:08:00.810 --> 00:08:02.590
which is obviously suboptimal normal,

00:08:02.590 --> 00:08:04.510
but I think things will get better.

00:08:04.510 --> 00:08:06.550
We've had a homeschooling
parent in the past say,

00:08:06.550 --> 00:08:08.020
just try to stick with it,

00:08:08.020 --> 00:08:10.420
it does get better, the
kids will get used to it.

00:08:10.420 --> 00:08:12.800
Obviously the suboptimal
situation for everyone.

00:08:12.800 --> 00:08:15.140
But the number one thing is
also take care of yourself.

00:08:15.140 --> 00:08:16.070
Don't get so overwhelmed.

00:08:16.070 --> 00:08:18.250
'Cause obviously the more as
parents we get overwhelmed

00:08:18.250 --> 00:08:19.390
and we'll snap at our children

00:08:19.390 --> 00:08:21.520
and then everyone will get stressed out.

00:08:21.520 --> 00:08:23.510
So the more that you
can kind of keep calm,

00:08:23.510 --> 00:08:24.670
whatever it does to get you know,

00:08:24.670 --> 00:08:25.660
whatever you do in your life

00:08:25.660 --> 00:08:27.570
to get to that meditative state,

00:08:27.570 --> 00:08:28.900
give yourself some alone time

00:08:28.900 --> 00:08:31.700
so that you'll have that emotional reserve

00:08:31.700 --> 00:08:33.870
to to deal with where the kids might

00:08:33.870 --> 00:08:35.320
the supports they might need.

00:08:37.290 --> 00:08:40.660
Fazlu from YouTube, Faizal Kabirin

00:08:40.660 --> 00:08:42.470
if I'm reading it correctly.

00:08:42.470 --> 00:08:44.150
This is a crucial moment of coronavirus,

00:08:44.150 --> 00:08:45.600
how can a student from Bangladesh

00:08:45.600 --> 00:08:47.380
continue his studies online?

00:08:47.380 --> 00:08:49.410
Okay, so it looks like
Fazul is from Bangladesh.

00:08:49.410 --> 00:08:52.563
Thanks for joining us, I
think a little late there.

00:08:54.100 --> 00:08:56.580
So you know depending
on your level of hussle,

00:08:56.580 --> 00:08:58.850
I think the the key is

00:08:58.850 --> 00:09:00.790
is that you actually you could view

00:09:00.790 --> 00:09:02.260
this as a glass-half-full scenario

00:09:02.260 --> 00:09:05.190
where a lot of the demands on your time,

00:09:05.190 --> 00:09:06.570
especially for younger students

00:09:06.570 --> 00:09:08.280
they might have had a
lot of social engagements

00:09:08.280 --> 00:09:10.860
and other extracurricular
activities or homework,

00:09:10.860 --> 00:09:12.570
a lot of those have been loosened

00:09:12.570 --> 00:09:16.160
and so a place that Khan
Academy is a great place

00:09:16.160 --> 00:09:18.930
to focus on those subjects

00:09:18.930 --> 00:09:19.960
that you really wanna make sure

00:09:19.960 --> 00:09:21.960
you have a strong foundation in,

00:09:21.960 --> 00:09:24.290
the high school subjects,
early college subjects,

00:09:24.290 --> 00:09:27.190
biology, chemistry, physics, economics

00:09:27.190 --> 00:09:28.023
there's other things off-site

00:09:28.023 --> 00:09:31.040
you know if you've graduated
outside of Khan Academy,

00:09:31.040 --> 00:09:32.570
you can move on to things like MOOCs

00:09:32.570 --> 00:09:35.840
and take more advanced
courses at a university level.

00:09:35.840 --> 00:09:38.700
I think it's a great
time to take on projects

00:09:38.700 --> 00:09:41.010
where it's one thing to learn
a lot of academic things

00:09:41.010 --> 00:09:42.820
but can you apply it, can you create

00:09:42.820 --> 00:09:46.920
you know can you know
create invent something

00:09:46.920 --> 00:09:49.940
that can solve problems for folks right,

00:09:49.940 --> 00:09:52.310
make a software application
that can do something.

00:09:52.310 --> 00:09:53.510
So I think there's a lot of opportunities

00:09:53.510 --> 00:09:54.920
but I think that's the best way

00:09:54.920 --> 00:09:57.540
to be constructively occupied right now.

00:09:57.540 --> 00:09:59.770
And obviously there might be
opportunities to volunteer

00:09:59.770 --> 00:10:00.900
for people in your community

00:10:00.900 --> 00:10:01.733
who might need help.

00:10:01.733 --> 00:10:02.960
If you're a young person,

00:10:02.960 --> 00:10:04.940
you are you should you have to

00:10:04.940 --> 00:10:06.600
you should be still socially distanced

00:10:06.600 --> 00:10:08.310
but you might be able to help older people

00:10:08.310 --> 00:10:10.610
who might have trouble
leaving their houses

00:10:10.610 --> 00:10:12.430
and have to be even more social distance

00:10:12.430 --> 00:10:14.330
you know with things
like getting groceries,

00:10:14.330 --> 00:10:16.000
or honestly just connecting with them.

00:10:16.000 --> 00:10:17.807
You know keep distance and say hello

00:10:17.807 --> 00:10:19.840
or send them a text message

00:10:19.840 --> 00:10:22.190
or just make sure they
feel socially connected.

