00:10:52.790 --> 00:10:54.380
if you just go to Khan Academy at all

00:10:54.380 --> 00:10:56.240
you'll see several links that say,

00:10:56.240 --> 00:10:57.920
daily schedules you click on that.

00:10:57.920 --> 00:11:00.670
I'm assuming y'all are maybe
high school aged students.

00:11:02.070 --> 00:11:03.330
But there's their schedules essentially

00:11:03.330 --> 00:11:06.140
for every age bucket high
school, middle school,

00:11:06.140 --> 00:11:08.260
elementary school and early learners.

00:11:08.260 --> 00:11:10.180
That's a good starting point,

00:11:10.180 --> 00:11:11.180
there's nothing rigid about those

00:11:11.180 --> 00:11:14.650
you can copy and paste it and
modify it to your own needs,

00:11:14.650 --> 00:11:16.310
but what I would advise is

00:11:16.310 --> 00:11:17.720
to have some form of a schedule

00:11:17.720 --> 00:11:19.540
and make sure your schedule gives you time

00:11:19.540 --> 00:11:21.000
to rest and relax.

00:11:21.000 --> 00:11:23.120
I think you know there's two extremes

00:11:23.120 --> 00:11:24.780
that people could fall into right now

00:11:24.780 --> 00:11:26.060
and it's completely fine to not have

00:11:26.060 --> 00:11:27.790
your act together in this
first or second week,

00:11:27.790 --> 00:11:32.260
but you know there could be the extreme

00:11:32.260 --> 00:11:34.450
where there's no structure

00:11:34.450 --> 00:11:37.550
and you're kind of just
wandering through your days,

00:11:37.550 --> 00:11:39.750
that doesn't feel healthy to me,

00:11:39.750 --> 00:11:41.770
after many days or weeks of that,

00:11:41.770 --> 00:11:46.000
you'll I think feel and a little
bit more blah so to speak.

00:11:46.000 --> 00:11:47.390
And then the other extreme we're like

00:11:47.390 --> 00:11:50.660
oh I got a study you know
18 hours a day and all that

00:11:50.660 --> 00:11:52.690
and that's going that is also unhealthy.

00:11:52.690 --> 00:11:55.310
So what I recommend is you
could use our schedules

00:11:55.310 --> 00:11:57.450
or create your own but
schedules that cover

00:11:57.450 --> 00:11:58.820
all the important basics,

00:11:58.820 --> 00:12:00.520
make sure there's time for gaps

00:12:00.520 --> 00:12:02.100
don't just try to power
through those gaps,

00:12:02.100 --> 00:12:03.690
I think especially now we need those gaps

00:12:03.690 --> 00:12:07.810
even more than ever and that
try to you know get front-load

00:12:07.810 --> 00:12:08.820
the work of your day,

00:12:08.820 --> 00:12:11.250
that's actually you know
how I try to do my life

00:12:11.250 --> 00:12:13.140
and then by early afternoon

00:12:13.140 --> 00:12:16.070
say okay I've done what
I need to do to the day,

00:12:16.070 --> 00:12:17.480
I can give myself a break

00:12:17.480 --> 00:12:21.790
and I can you know
entertain myself watch TV,

00:12:21.790 --> 00:12:24.400
or work on a project
that I really care about,

00:12:24.400 --> 00:12:28.220
I can do a little bit of video
conferencing with friends

00:12:28.220 --> 00:12:29.560
and you know there's always this question

00:12:29.560 --> 00:12:31.690
about FaceTime screen time

00:12:31.690 --> 00:12:33.880
and I think there's good
and there's bad screen time

00:12:33.880 --> 00:12:36.940
and actually even with sometimes
bad screen time is okay.

00:12:36.940 --> 00:12:39.890
Now that we we're
finding more time at home

00:12:39.890 --> 00:12:42.770
but the good screen time is
or the better screen time

00:12:42.770 --> 00:12:44.140
is especially for an older student

00:12:44.140 --> 00:12:47.470
is your time learning,
your time creating, writing

00:12:47.470 --> 00:12:50.020
coding and I think it's a valuable time

00:12:50.020 --> 00:12:52.530
to get on a videoconference zoom

00:12:52.530 --> 00:12:56.440
or a Google meet or hangout
or Skype FaceTime with friends

00:12:56.440 --> 00:12:58.570
and and I encourage you,

00:12:58.570 --> 00:13:01.140
you know don't just try
to go a little bit deeper,

00:13:01.140 --> 00:13:02.290
talk to your friends about what

00:13:02.290 --> 00:13:03.200
what are you really thinking about,

00:13:03.200 --> 00:13:04.130
what are they stressed about,

00:13:04.130 --> 00:13:05.260
what are they anxious about

00:13:05.260 --> 00:13:07.620
and remind your friends that
you're here to support them

00:13:07.620 --> 00:13:10.043
'cause I think we all need
to hear that right now.

