00:13:58.160 --> 00:14:02.700
And so I think Nina was the
name if I heard correctly,

00:14:02.700 --> 00:14:04.360
but what I encourage you to do

00:14:04.360 --> 00:14:06.640
is go to that official free SAT practice

00:14:06.640 --> 00:14:08.640
on Khan Academy you can
navigate on Khan Academy

00:14:08.640 --> 00:14:10.870
or just do a web search
SAT practice Khan Academy

00:14:10.870 --> 00:14:13.550
you'll find it and you get started

00:14:13.550 --> 00:14:15.650
and try to spend equal
amounts of time in math,

00:14:15.650 --> 00:14:17.630
reading, math and reading especially

00:14:17.630 --> 00:14:19.620
and also time on writing.

00:14:19.620 --> 00:14:20.900
What we've seen in the data

00:14:20.900 --> 00:14:23.430
is the best practices for students are

00:14:23.430 --> 00:14:25.830
make sure you are working on skills

00:14:25.830 --> 00:14:27.980
that are pushing you forward

00:14:27.980 --> 00:14:29.570
and you're not just
trying to do easy things.

00:14:29.570 --> 00:14:31.570
Oh there you go very good.

00:14:31.570 --> 00:14:34.540
We're getting better at this
technology all the time.

00:14:34.540 --> 00:14:37.710
Try to peer you know
follow the recommendations.

00:14:37.710 --> 00:14:40.540
The recommendations we
actually the software

00:14:40.540 --> 00:14:42.160
in partnership with the SAT folks,

00:14:42.160 --> 00:14:45.750
it knows which concepts are most important

00:14:45.750 --> 00:14:50.750
for not just for the SAT but
also for college readiness

00:14:51.170 --> 00:14:55.130
and also it knows where
your weak spots are.

00:14:55.130 --> 00:14:57.740
So as you answer more and more questions,

00:14:57.740 --> 00:14:59.730
it will know your strengths
and your weaknesses.

00:14:59.730 --> 00:15:01.430
And so it's trying to
give you the suggestions

00:15:01.430 --> 00:15:04.160
that are optimal for you to
learn as much as possible.

00:15:04.160 --> 00:15:06.050
If you've taken the PSAT,

00:15:06.050 --> 00:15:09.350
