00:16:44.480 --> 00:16:47.560
- So Sal our next question
is fun from YouTube

00:16:47.560 --> 00:16:51.180
by Prag Yamaha, her question is

00:16:52.090 --> 00:16:54.310
hello how is it important to make notes

00:16:54.310 --> 00:16:55.733
each time we watch a video?

00:16:57.930 --> 00:17:00.510
- I think notes can be valuable.

00:17:00.510 --> 00:17:03.440
I think the most important
thing when you watch a video

00:17:03.440 --> 00:17:05.800
is to try to do it in an active way.

00:17:05.800 --> 00:17:09.410
So if the video is about to
go through a worked example,

00:17:09.410 --> 00:17:11.460
pause the video, try to solve it

00:17:11.460 --> 00:17:13.210
at least attempt it yourself.

00:17:13.210 --> 00:17:16.210
If the video is about to explain

00:17:16.210 --> 00:17:19.630
the stages of mitosis for
example if in your biology,

00:17:19.630 --> 00:17:20.910
try to think about it yourself.

00:17:20.910 --> 00:17:22.340
Say okay do what do I know about it,

00:17:22.340 --> 00:17:23.390
what do I don't know about it.

00:17:23.390 --> 00:17:25.700
So you get your brain primed.

00:17:25.700 --> 00:17:27.690
Then on top of that I think it is useful

00:17:27.690 --> 00:17:29.350
for a lot of folks to take notes.

00:17:29.350 --> 00:17:32.923
It helps kind of multiple
modalities to do that.

00:17:34.040 --> 00:17:36.490
You know but for other people

00:17:36.490 --> 00:17:38.370
it might be more useful
to just really make sure

00:17:38.370 --> 00:17:40.090
they're focused on what's being said.

00:17:40.090 --> 00:17:42.120
I think sometimes notes can kind of be

00:17:42.120 --> 00:17:44.470
kind of a blind process too.

00:17:44.470 --> 00:17:47.330
So the more that you can take notes

00:17:47.330 --> 00:17:48.400
but when you take the notes,

00:17:48.400 --> 00:17:49.710
you're really processing.

00:17:49.710 --> 00:17:51.100
So you're not just writing verbatim

00:17:51.100 --> 00:17:52.290
or drawing verbatim.

00:17:52.290 --> 00:17:53.720
You're looking at what's happening

00:17:53.720 --> 00:17:55.910
and this is true whether
it's a video or a classroom.

00:17:55.910 --> 00:17:57.810
You're like okay now let me process that

00:17:57.810 --> 00:17:59.730
and digest it in my own words,

00:17:59.730 --> 00:18:01.380
I think that could be a lot more valuable.

00:18:01.380 --> 00:18:03.290
The important thing is
to really pay attention

00:18:03.290 --> 00:18:05.650
and the beauty of videos
is you can pause it

00:18:05.650 --> 00:18:08.190
and say okay do I really get that,

00:18:08.190 --> 00:18:10.400
how would I do it etc.

00:18:10.400 --> 00:18:11.790
And then you can you can play

00:18:11.790 --> 00:18:14.250
and see how the the Video Creator

00:18:14.250 --> 00:18:16.163
has approached the concept.

